      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Respectfully, this isn't a feature request, it's a bug. Avatar cameras should show the same things as any other camera. As a world creator, when I turn on depth through udon, it's because the world has shaders that need it while avoiding an expensive shadow pass. It's expected to turn on depth in all cameras, including avatar cameras. Unfortunately, many worlds are still using a directional light because of this bug, and that causes a lot of unnecessary draw calls.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-08-12T13:12:39.270Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "https://creators.vrchat.com/worlds/udon/vrc-graphics/vrc-camera-settings/\n\nScreenCamera.DepthTextureMode and PhotoCamera.DepthTextureMode don't enable depth generation on cameras attached to an avatar.\n\nInstead, avatar cameras use a previous [and invalid] depth buffer rendered by ScreenCamera or PhotoCamera, which leads to off-axis depth effects in shaders rendered with these cameras.\n\nThis produces artifacts and broken shader behavior with third party camera systems like VRCLens, etc, in worlds that utilize DepthTextureMode instead of a depth light.",
